    "settings": "Sony A7R III · Sony FE 70-200mm F2.8 GM OSS II · 200mm · 1/1250s · f/2.8 · ISO 100",
    "note": "200mm is the reach the 70-200mm has, and for wildlife it's the minimum I like: it fills the frame without approaching closer than is comfortable for the animal. Wide open at f/2.8, the background forest goes soft and the second elk becomes a suggestion rather than a distraction. 1/1250s freezes any movement of the head or ears and rules out shake at 200mm. ISO 100 keeps the dark forest clean, which matters when so much of the frame is deep shadow.",
    "date": "2026-10-09"
