    "note": "At 35mm, the long end of the 16-35mm, I could fit the full skyline and plenty of sky without making the city look tiny. f/9 keeps everything sharp, from the water in front to the towers and the clouds. Bright daylight gave 1/800s at ISO 125, which freezes the sailboat and the texture of the water. Base ISO keeps the large areas of blue sky smooth.",
    "date": "2026-10-09"
